Changes needed to build Poppler for wasm32-wasip1.

Kept outside third_party/poppler so the submodule stays a pristine upstream checkout and
bumping it is a one-line pin change. Prefer CMake options over patching; this file is for
what configuration cannot express. Both changes below are plain upstream bugs that surface
on WASI first, not WASI-specific workarounds, so they are upstreamable and this file should
shrink to nothing.

1. goo/gfile.cc: drop the unused <pwd.h> include.
   wasi-libc has no user database, so the include is a hard build failure. Nothing in
   Poppler references getpwnam/getpwuid/struct passwd -- this was the only mention of pwd.h
   in the tree -- so removing it is a no-op everywhere.

2. poppler/Object.h: take std::unique_ptr<Array> by rvalue reference, not by value.
   By value instantiates std::default_delete<Array>::operator() where Array is only forward
   declared. libc++ makes ~unique_ptr constexpr for C++23 and Poppler sets
   CMAKE_CXX_STANDARD 23, so the "cannot delete an incomplete type" static_assert fires,
   breaking 71 of 84 core translation units. The neighbouring Dict and Stream constructors
   already take &&, every call site already passes an rvalue, and unique_ptr is not
   copyable, so no caller can be affected. Reproduces for any libc++ build at C++23.

diff --git a/goo/gfile.cc b/goo/gfile.cc
index 32e892b6..56f79313 100644
--- a/goo/gfile.cc
+++ b/goo/gfile.cc
@@ -43,7 +43,6 @@
 #    include <sys/stat.h>
 #    include <fcntl.h>
 #    include <cstring>
-#    include <pwd.h>
 #endif // _WIN32
 #include <cstdio>
 #include <limits>
diff --git a/poppler/Object.h b/poppler/Object.h
index eac2f5a4..e60d2094 100644
--- a/poppler/Object.h
+++ b/poppler/Object.h
@@ -149,7 +149,7 @@ public:
 
     explicit Object(long long int64gA) : type { objInt64 }, data { int64gA } { }
 
-    explicit Object(std::unique_ptr<Array> arrayA) : type { objArray }, data { std::shared_ptr<Array>(std::move(arrayA)) } { }
+    explicit Object(std::unique_ptr<Array> &&arrayA) : type { objArray }, data { std::shared_ptr<Array>(std::move(arrayA)) } { }
 
     explicit Object(std::unique_ptr<Dict> &&dictA) : type { objDict }, data { std::shared_ptr<Dict>(std::move(dictA)) } { }
 
